Tanzania Citizenship Application Procedures
- Fill the required application forms;
- Submit the forms to your local Ward Executive Secretary or Sheha (in Zanzibar);
- The local official will forward the file to the District Immigration Office. At this stage, you will be required to pay a non-refundable submission fee of USD 1,500;
- Publish a "Notice of Intention to Apply for Naturalization" in two consecutive issues of registered daily newspapers in both Mainland Tanzania and Zanzibar;
- Attend a formal interview conducted by the District Defense and Security Committee;
- The District Immigration Officer sends the application to the Regional Immigration Officer, who then presents it to the Regional Defense and Security Committee for detailed review;
- The Regional Immigration Officer submits the application to the Commissioner General of Immigration for a formal recommendation to the Minister.
- For the case of Zanzibar before the application is sent to the Commissioner General of Immigration, the Commissioner of Immigration Zanzibar forwards the application to the office of the Second Vice President for recommendation and it is later submitted to the Commissioner General of Immigration for his recommendation to the Minister.
- The Commissioner General of Immigration forwards the recommended application to the Minister for final decision.
NB:
For applications originating in Zanzibar, the Commissioner of Immigration Zanzibar must first forward the file to the Office of the Second Vice President for recommendation before it reaches the Commissioner General.
Final Decision: The Commissioner General forwards the recommended application to the Minister, who makes the final decision on the grant of citizenship.

