✓ Other purposes which may be covered by an Ordinary Visa include attending a meeting, visiting friends or relatives, and participating in a workshop or exhibition;
✓ Holders of an Ordinary Visa are not permitted to work or conduct any business.
Requirements i. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
ii. Return ticket;
iii. Duly filled in application and declaration form available online;
iv. Respective visa fee payment.

A Business Visa may be issued for a period not exceeding 90 days to foreign nationals who wish to enter the United Republic of Tanzania for one of the following purposes:
✓ To conduct special assignments such as fixing or repairing machines, or to run short term training;
✓ To conduct short term professional assignments such as auditing, making feasibility studies, conducting professional jobs, establishing business contacts, or making arrangements for investments during the start-up period of the company;
✓ To conduct any other short term lawful business -related task recognized by the laws of the country and as may be determined by the issuing authority.
Important Note for Business Visa ✓ The maximum validity for a Business Visa is 90 days;
✓ A Business Visa is issued on a single entry basis. It cannot be used to re -enter the country after the holder leaves the country;
✓ The Business Visa should not be used in lieu of a Residence Permit. If for any reason the activity or intended assignment will exceed 3 months, an applicant is advised to apply for a Work or Residence Permit instead of a Business Visa.
Requirements i. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
ii. Return ticket;
iii. 250 USD visa fee;
iv. A work contract or any proof of the work or assignment to be performed within a period not exceeding three months.

✓ A Multiple Visa may be issued to American nationals (due to bilateral agreements between Tanzania and America) who wish to come for such purposes as holiday or tourism, visiting friends and relatives, or attending a conference. American nationals are not entitled to an Ordinary Visa; this implies that USA passport holders who wish to visit Tanzania for tourism or holiday MUST apply for a Multiple Visa even if they plan for a single entry;
✓ A Multiple Visa may also be issued to Directors of companies registered in Tanzania who do not reside in the country, persons engaging in bilateral meetings, spouses married to Tanzanians or residents, Government consultants, representatives of international NGOs, and any other person as may be determined by the Commissioner General of Immigration;
✓ Non-resident Directors MUST upload a BRELA SEARCH document to prove that they are Directors of a company registered in Tanzania (BRELA is the competent authority responsible for registration of companies in Tanzania);
✓ Applicants for a Multiple Visa under the umbrella of projects or bilateral meetings with Government Ministries or Institutions should obtain an application letter from the respective Government Ministry or Institution, and upload such letters in their appl ications. Failure to observe this procedure may cause their applications to be rejected;
✓ Applicants for a Multiple Visa under the family visit category are required to upload proof of relationship with their family members. In this case, a certificate of marriage (for proof of relationship with regard to spouses) or birth certificates (for pro of of relationship with regard to children) is required;
✓ Duration and validity of a Multiple Visa: it may be issued for a maximum validity of twelve (12) months. However, the maximum consecutive stay in the country is only three months. This means

the holder of a Multiple Visa cannot stay in the country for twel ve (12) consecutive months.
Instead, on each visit a holder may stay in the country for a maximum period of three months (90 days).
Requirements: Multiple Visa (Non-Resident Director) i. A recent passport size photo of the applicant;
ii. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
iii. Return ticket;
iv. A covering letter from the company;
v. A copy of the registration certificate or certificate of compliance of the company;
vi. BRELA SEARCH document (proof of being a Director from BRELA);
vii. 100 USD visa fee.
Requirements: Multiple Visa (Consultancy with Government Ministries / Bilateral Agreements) i. A recent passport size photo of the applicant;
ii. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
iii. Return ticket of the flight;
iv. A covering letter from the respective Government Ministry or Institution; OR a covering letter from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and East African Cooperation describing the bilateral agreement;
v. 100 USD visa fee.
Requirements: Multiple Visa (Family Visit) i. A recent passport size photo of the applicant;
ii. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
iii. Return ticket of the flight;
iv. An invitation letter from the spouse or child to whom the visit is made;
v. Attached marriage certificate (if the applicant visits a spouse), or birth certificate (if the applicant visits his child or children);
vi. Valid passport or national ID of the spouse or child if applicable, or a valid Residence Permit if the spouse or child is a resident;
vii. 100 USD visa fee.
Requirements: Multiple Visa (USA Nationals Visiting for Holiday or Tourism) i. A recent passport size photo of the applicant;
ii. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);

iii. Return ticket of the flight;
iv. 100 USD visa fee.
Requirements: Multiple Visa (Others) Any Multiple Visa applied for online which does not fall in the categories indicated above MUST be supported by the following attachments:
i. A recent passport size photo of the applicant;
ii. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
iii. A permission letter from the Commissioner General of Immigration or the Commissioner of Immigration, Zanzibar;
iv. Return ticket of the flight;
v. 100 USD visa fee.

This Visa may be issued to foreign nationals who seek to enter the country on transit to other countries.
It is issued for a period not exceeding seven days. The applicant for this visa may be required to provide proof of a Visa of the destination country and/or an onward ticket.
NB: A Transit Visa is strictly intended for travellers whose purpose of entry is transiting through Tanzania to another country. It is not meant for tourism or any purpose other than transit.
Requirements i. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
ii. 30 USD visa fee;
iii. An entry visa and/or onward ticket to the intended country of destination.

A Student Visa may be issued to a foreign national who wishes to enter the country for academic purposes such as research, internship, volunteering, students under an exchange programme and prospective students who have obtained admission in registered institutions in Tanzania.
The validity of this Visa is grouped in two main categories. The first category is for applicants whose academic programmes do not exceed 90 days, for which the visa fee is 50 USD. The second category is for those whose academic programmes exceed 90 days, for which the visa fee is 250 USD.
Applicants whose countries do not require a Visa to enter Tanzania, and who wish to come for academic purposes, will have to apply for a Student Pass.
NB: The validity of a Visa for applicants who wish to undertake language courses will not exceed six months.
Requirements i. Copy of the applicant’s valid passport (biographic data page);
ii. 50 USD, 250 USD or 550 USD visa fee depending on the category and duration;
iii. Covering letter from the host institution or college where the foreign student will be hosted; the letter must detail the course or field and the duration of the programme to be attended;
iv. An open return ticket.
